      "writtenOn": "2021-07-12T17:39:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, based on the Bazel behavior, which since we\u0027re transitioning to it, a similar syntax would be advantageous.\n\nBut I also so that because the `:` within a fully qualified reference serves the same purpose as a leading `:`  as it indicates which module name we are referring to.\n\nAs far as I know, all references about this refer to :module-name, which doesn\u0027t mention fully-qualified names, and fully-qualified names have never worked, so it\u0027s  a new feature, we don\u0027t have to shoe-horn it in.\n\nIt should just be a small matter of updating SrcIsModule and SrcIsModuleWithTag to handle a fully-qualified path",
